#ifdef PAM_AUTHENTICATION_MODULE
auth sufficient PAM_AUTHENTICATION_MODULE
#endif
auth required pam_unix.so
-auth optional pam_gnome_keyring.so

account required pam_nologin.so
account required pam_unix.so

XCOMM Not every system ships pam_lastlog, pam_systemd or pam_gnome_keyring: a missing module is not an error.
-session optional pam_lastlog.so
-session optional pam_systemd.so
-session optional pam_gnome_keyring.so auto_start

XCOMM The password section is used when the account check reports that the
XCOMM password has expired and the user sets a new one in the login screen.
password required pam_unix.so obscure
-password optional pam_gnome_keyring.so
